the eve of summer game fest is upon us  yet as we sit ready to bask in the sunny  glow of game trailers news and  announcements there is one former gaming  event giant that won't be part of the  festivities  e3 the electronic gaming expo which  began in 1995 sadly announced it was  canceling its 2022 event leaving us only  with our memories yet e3 has given us  numerous memorable moments and memes  from its two decades of history so today  we're shouting out some of our favorites  fair warning there are a lot of cringes  ahead  back in 2006 sony felt like leonardo  dicaprio in titanic  the playstation 2 had not only managed  to unseat the king of the gaming world  nintendo but also managed to hold off  microsoft's upstart xbox to become the  best-selling console of all time however  this domination perhaps led to some  overconfidence on the part of sony as  when it came time to announce the  console's successor sony chairman  kazurai took to the stage to announce  that the playstation 3 would cost an  astounding  599 dollars causing the room to  instantly fall silent the 20 gigabyte  playstation 3 will retail for  499 us dollars and 549 canadian dollars  and the 60 gigabyte playstation 3 for  599 us dollars  659 dollars canadian it's one of the  most shocking moments in e3 history made  even worse by the fact that microsoft's  xbox 360 was retailing at 399 dollars at  its most expensive tier in part leading  the 360 to dominate the early part of  that generation sales a lead that  playstation 3 would take years to  eventually surpass  [Music]  yet it's not just sony that fell victim  to overconfidence because in 2013 sony  got its revenge on microsoft earlier  that year microsoft had unveiled its  latest console the xbox one and its  reveal left gamers with a bad taste in  their mouth not only had the company  seemingly ignored its core audience of  gamers by focusing almost entirely on  the console's more multimedia  possibilities but its worst offense to  many was its aggressive drm policy that  would not only require the system to be  always online in order for people to  play games on it but would also allow  publishers to entirely kill sharing and  buying used games as a result microsoft  came to e3 with little public goodwill  behind them something sony took  advantage of during their press  conference sony released a hilarious  instructional video featuring execs adam  boyce and shuhei yoshida on how to share  games on their new playstation 4. this  is how you share your games on ps4  [Music]  thanks  please  it was an entirely simple yet knockout  punch that won sony the early momentum  in the latest gaming generations  mindshare  speaking of knockouts though keanu  reeves whether he's stopping a bus with  sandra bullock beating up fascist  computer elrond or avenging puppies with  endless violence we stand keanu reeves  here and that sentiment is clearly  shared by many gamers causing one of the  best moments at e3 2019 when keanu  reeves graced the stage during  microsoft's xbox event to reveal that he  would be appearing in cyberpunk 2077 as  johnny silverhand leading to this  beautiful exchange with an audience  member the feeling of of being there of  walking the streets of the future  is really going to be breathtaking  you're breathtaking  you're all breathtaking  all right all right all right so  not only do we agree about keanu's  breathtaking capabilities but this  adorable moment also proved exactly why  back in the early 2000s grand theft auto  was the king of gaming though  i guess that hasn't really changed  however the juggernaut gta franchise had  become synonymous with the playstation  with its initial exclusive releases for  gta 3 and vice city on the playstation 2  which made it all the more shocking when  xbox's peter moore took the stage in  2006 and rolled up his sleeve to reveal  his newest tattoo the grand theft auto  iv logo announcing that gta 4 was coming  to xbox and even had exclusive dlc but  it gets even better  microsoft and rockstar games have  entered into a strategic partnership to  provide exclusive  episodic content  via xbox live  sadly e3 moments are not always  remembered for how great they were  sometimes  they're remembered for being much much  worse  it's ridge racer  ridge racer in 2010 ubisoft was  seemingly riding high yet during the  middle of its press conference hosted by  community's own joel mchale it decided  to create one of the cringiest moments  in e3 history by having players run  around the crowd playing laser tag to  promote their then upcoming real world  shooter game battle tag it's attractive  people running around  um  [Music]  [Music]  it's deeply  deeply painful made even worse by the  fact that its e3 moment made more of an  impression than the game ever did  yet while ubisoft certainly has had  terrible moments at e3 it definitely  hasn't hit the lows of konami in 2010.  konami's entire press conference that  year was front to back one of the most  painful viewing experiences of our lives  and i can't even imagine what it must  have been like to be in the room i won't  put you through the hell of a beat by  beat discussion but some of the  highlights include live luchador  performers awkwardly interrupting one of  the publishers talking let's leave  now yeah  a group of karaoke singers performing  show tunes for glee karaoke revolution  and takifuji trying to get applause from  a deeply uncomfortable audience with  some of the worst lines in e3 history  hi  [Applause]  and also you'll see the that the  difficulty levels will be changed on a  two players mode and making  even harder  speaking of cringe though we'd be remiss  if we didn't let nintendo enter the  competition in 2008 during nintendo's  conference the iconic shigeru miyamoto  took to the stage to help promote the  latest game in the endlessly successful  wii games line this time wii music and  he and several others decided to play a  performance for the audience in the game  and  well  the music speaks for itself doesn't it  [Music]  perhaps this moment is why no one is  clambering for a wee music revival in  the same way we got a wii sports revival  for the switch well i'm here to say i'm  calling them out as cowards bring me wee  music switch  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  unfortunately wii music wasn't  miyamoto's only cringe e3 moment on this  list two years after the wii music  fiasco miyamoto once again stepped onto  the stage to promote the return of the  iconic zelda franchise with skyward  sword and like many games on the wii the  biggest overt change to the series  formula came with its addition of motion  controls promising to let you swing and  slash like link himself however when  miyamoto tried to show off how cool it  would be he ended up recreating a more  realistic portrayal of most players  experiences with the wii flailing about  as the controller refused to respond to  his inputs  and if i do a shield bash  then i can knock the rocks back at him  [Laughter]  there we go  thankfully years later skyward sword  made the motion control optional in its  switch re-release allowing people a  chance to re-experience the game without  worry of  wireless interference  alright we've been kind of harsh on  miyamoto but while he's certainly had  his awkward moments at e3 he's also  delivered one of its most heartwarming  and e3 2017 miyamoto appeared at  ubisoft's conference to discuss  nintendo's collaboration with the  company with the game mario plus rabbits  kingdom battle it's not every day that  one of gaming's biggest figures talks  about a game you helped create and  creative director david solani certainly  felt the profoundness of the moment  getting emotional as miyamoto discussed  the game  so when i met davide-san who is the  creative director of this game  yes  when i  when i met davideson i had just  just one condition for this project  [Applause]  it's one of the earnest and sweetest  moments in all of e3  but that's our list for some of the best  moments in e3 history but obviously  there are so many more from cliffy b's  gear's war announcement to whatever the  hell usher was doing here  so let us know what some of your  favorite moments from e3 were down in  the comments and if you're done  reminiscing don't forget to subscribe to  gamespot for all our impending summer  games fest coverage otherwise thanks for  watching  [Music]
 

